{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Local full-surface run caught two real regressions that CI would have flagged, now fixed\nin patch set 4 of Gerrit change 2093.\n\nBoth are deliberate \"re-approval\" pins that record the approved code-review blocking set as\na literal and exist precisely so that growing it cannot happen silently:\n- tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py::test_secrets_security_keys_are_the_ws5_blocking_handoff\n- tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py::test_code_review_approved_blocking_criteria_set\n\nRouting `correctness` and `edge-cases` blocking takes the set from eight to ten, so both pins\nwere updated to the ten-criterion set with the measurement recorded as the rationale. That is\nthe mechanism working as designed, not a test being bent to fit: the pin's whole purpose is to\nforce this to be an explicit, justified change.\n\nEvidence: 75 routing-relevant test modules (every tests/*.py referencing blocking_enabled,\neffective_criteria, routing_index, threshold_for or criteria_routing) -- 1355 passed, the 2\nfailures above, plus 1 error in test_asserted_capability_criterion.py that was a `git`\nsubprocess TimeoutExpired under heavy machine contention; that module passes 8/8 in isolation,\nso it is environmental, not a code fault.\n\nAfter the fix: those two modules plus the new test file pass 40/40; make lint PASS; make\ntypecheck PASS; complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787387595519017001,"uuid":"ecb1fb42-3466-492e-acae-c7fe37df9ce8"}